I think you are correct that Nethack requires "careful judgment and
compromise" everywhere, even in the mid and late game. The reason is
that, as personal proficiency increases, one is willing to accept less
equipment/stats/etc., thus situations may become challenging that you
wouldn't care of if you had, say, optimal enchanted weapon and armor,
a HP buffer of several hundred points, maxed stats, and everything.
But whether you accept less equipment to ascend or collect some more
items and stats in the usual ("hard") way, finding a farm (or farming
yourself) will always make an essential part of the game meaningless.

